ion, the company provides smart inbox, comprehensive case management, social customer relationship management, social monitoring and alerts, customer service tools, and automation; and centralized content planning, creation, and publishing, automated scheduling, content performance reporting, suggested content, message approval workflows, publishing permissions and governance, and content and asset libraries. Further, it offers social media; content performance, customer service and team, custom report builder, and reporting API; and market research, brand health, competitive insights, consumer trends, and product feedback; and reputation and review management, mobile applications, and chat bot creation and management. Additionally, the company offers professional services consisting of consulting and training services. It serves social and community management; public relations; marketing; influencer marketing; customer service and care; commerce, sales and customer acquisition; recruiting and hiring, product development, and business strategy; and small-and-medium-sized businesses, mid-market companies, enterprises, marketing agencies, government, non-profit, and educational institutions. The company was incorporated in 2010 and is headquartered in Chicago, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ryan Paul Barretto | President, CEO, Director & Interim Principal Financial and Accounting Officer | Age 45 | Compensation: $966,837 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $336K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 28%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $29K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $58K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Sprout Social, Inc is a small-cap technology business with a $685M market cap on $458M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +22% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -59% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 77% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $39M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -17.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 79% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7918600338807505},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(SPT) Volatility Zones as Tactical Triggers","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/10/SPT_Volatility_Zones_as_Tactical_Triggers_111326050402_1794607442.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794607442.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing HeartCore Enterprises (NASDAQ:HTCR) & Sprout Social (NASDAQ:SPT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/reviewing-heartcore-enterprises-nasdaqhtcr-sprout-social-nasdaqspt.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794074330.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.943,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Analyzing Sprout Social (NASDAQ:SPT) and Banzai International (NASDAQ:BNZI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/analyzing-sprout-social-nasdaqspt-and-banzai-international-nasdaqbnzi.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794029327.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Barclays Forecasts Strong Price Appreciation for Sprout Social (NASDAQ:SPT) Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.co